---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="MeetPaw — Privacy Policy" description="How MeetPaw handles your data: everything stays on your Mac." path="/privacy">
<main class="doc">
  <a class="back" href="/">← MeetPaw</a>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 11 October 2026</p>

  <p>MeetPaw is an open-source macOS menu-bar app. It runs entirely on your Mac. The short version: your data stays on your device.</p>

  <h2>What MeetPaw accesses</h2>
  <p>With your explicit consent through sign-in, MeetPaw uses provider permissions to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Create instant and scheduled meetings (Google Meet, Zoom, Microsoft Teams).</li>
    <li>Read your upcoming calendar meetings so you can join them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What MeetPaw stores</h2>
  <p>Your access and refresh tokens are stored locally in your Mac's <b>Keychain</b>. Meeting and calendar data is held only in memory while the app runs and is never written to disk by MeetPaw.</p>

  <h2>What MeetPaw does <em>not</em> do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No data is sent to the developer or any third-party server — MeetPaw talks only to Google, Zoom, and Microsoft, directly from your Mac.</li>
    <li>No analytics, no tracking, no advertising.</li>
    <li>No selling or sharing of any data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Revoking access</h2>
  <p>Sign out in the app at any time (this deletes the stored tokens), or revoke access from your provider's account settings
     (<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google</a>, Zoom, or Microsoft).</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/meetnazreen/meetpaw">GitHub</a>.</p>
</main>
<style is:global>
